            <ArticleTitle>What Taiwan contributes to the world of allergy and clinical immunology?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5415/apallergy.2013.3.4.209</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In commemorate the 9th Asia Pacific Congress of Allergy, Asthma, and Clinical Immunology (APCAACI) in Taipei, Taiwan in November this year, some of the seminar works and contributions by the researchers from Taiwan to the advance in the field of allergy and clinical immunology, such as DNA vaccine, traditional Chinese medicine, anti-IgE antibody, and personalized medicine for severe drug allergic reaction, are summarized in this special review.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
